UPDATE public.designers
SET
  biography = $$Founded in Bordeaux, SOLLEN is a French designer-furniture publishing house born from a dialogue between designers and artisans. The young maison conceives elegant, timeless pieces — seating, tables, daybeds and lighting — produced locally in partnership with workshops recognised for exceptional savoir-faire, including the Lécuiller company, France's leading specialist in moulded wood for sixty years, and the Bastiat workshop, perpetuating the art of upholstery since 1964.

https://youtu.be/oHx35m3gkSg | Sollen — Brand Film | right | poster:https://img.youtube.com/vi/oHx35m3gkSg/hqdefault.jpg

Several of these partner ateliers carry the prestigious Entreprise du Patrimoine Vivant (Living Heritage Company) label and also serve France's leading luxury houses.

SOLLEN develops its collections in close collaboration with award-winning French designers — among them Arthur and Didier Garrigos of the Garrigos Design agency — to deliver furniture that combines comfort, refined design and sculptural aesthetics.

https://res.cloudinary.com/dif1oamtj/image/upload/v1777981450/Screenshot_2026-05-05_at_7.43.31_PM_dhxhil.png | Arthur Garros at work | left

The maison made its first appearance at Maison&Objet Paris in January 2023, unveiling the NUAGE (Cloud) collection in a poetic scenography signed by sculptor and paper artist Junior Fritz Jacquet, and has since participated in Paris Design Week at Galerie Joseph and in France Design Week 2023 at La Crèmerie showroom in Bordeaux.

https://res.cloudinary.com/dif1oamtj/image/upload/v1777981451/Screenshot_2026-05-05_at_7.43.17_PM_k8gbki.png | Cloud Wood Armchair Drawings | right$$,
  biography_images = '{}'::text[]
